1,Chong - cog (Austro-Asiatic) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/cog/,"Chong (cog) is part of the Austro-Asiatic family and Austro-Asiatic, Mon-Khmer, Eastern Mon-Khmer, Pearic, Western, Chong class.",Chong,Austro-Asiatic
2,Austro-Asiatic Language Family - Structure & Dialects - MustGo,https://www-mustgo-com.nproxy.org/worldlanguages/austro-asiatic-language-family/,"The Austro-Asiatic language family consists of 169 languages spoken in Southeast Asia, in countries located between China and Indonesia. A few are spoken to the west of this area in the Nicobar Islands and in India. The austro– part of the name comes from the Latin word for ‘south.’",Chong,Austro-Asiatic
3,"Austroasiatic languages | Mon-Khmer, Munda & Vietic | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/topic/Austroasiatic-languages,"Austroasiatic languages, stock of some 150 languages spoken by more than 65 million people scattered throughout Southeast Asia and eastern India. Most of these languages have numerous dialects.",Chong,Austro-Asiatic
